      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If short breaks aren't enough, you might need a more sustainable way to engage with the noise, rather than trying to stop it completely. Consider grounding techniques that involve deep, slow breathing while naming objects you can see, touch, or hear. This shifts your focus from the overwhelming internal chatter to the immediate, manageable reality around you. Remember, it's about managing the volume, not eliminating the sound entirely.",
